{"title":"MIE 2016","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Note: Anyone that solve any of the problems can post your solutions.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_1_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_2_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Problem_3_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Problem_4_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#Problem_5_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-19\"><a href=\"#Problem_6_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-20\"><a href=\"#Problem_7_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-21\"><a href=\"#Problem_8_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-22\"><a href=\"#Problem_9_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-23\"><a href=\"#Problem_10_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Choose the correct answer.\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/d/78d8f45fbff00e3efcf7a1dc9214deeacd596cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2016}-\\sqrt{2015}&lt;\\sqrt{2017}-\\sqrt{2016}&lt;(2\\sqrt{2016})^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c1ab3e8d40cd7e02da41f8336b325b02c94f544.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2017}-\\sqrt{2016}&lt;\\sqrt{2016}-\\sqrt{2015}&lt;(2\\sqrt{2016})^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/7/c07786d8ae77d223bd0598dc945476e46ff7e1e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2017}-\\sqrt{2016}&lt;(2\\sqrt{2016})^{-1}&lt;\\sqrt{2016}-\\sqrt{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/a/85a621eed71f639fbe52ad7b9f5f2a13532d5680.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2016}-\\sqrt{2015}&lt;(2\\sqrt{2016})^{-1}&lt;\\sqrt{2017}-\\sqrt{2016}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/c/85c545ffe8a4dbd270022aed32cef732dd0dfcf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2\\sqrt{2016})^{-1}&lt;\\sqrt{2017}-\\sqrt{2016}&lt;\\sqrt{2016}-\\sqrt{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016/Problem_1\" title=\"MIE 2016/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The following system has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> integer solutions. We can say that:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b03ed0218784e2a44c146af69dcb43a0e55f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{cases}\\frac{x^2-2x-14}{x}&gt;3\\\\\\\\x\\leq12\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"114\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fcab1b2fcb409eda856956d0d11b1a5330ded3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq k\\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/7/547e5dd37a024136d990b0996d8829269c236c8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\leq k\\leq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/1437ae61a7e5566e0b4901710d132254e48e5cd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\leq k\\leq6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/4/504ac467036dda6dea24d2d3e43f47e018240e6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\leq k\\leq8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82681964dc24de82892ae5e51400219fb0c652b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016/Day_1/Problem_2\" title=\"MIE 2016/Day 1/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28c367151db654c98df81eb7ab6e1d72b4233f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e2f6d8f31beacce2d10c823fa4d68e278e8f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be complex numbers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e2f6d8f31beacce2d10c823fa4d68e278e8f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> is a pure imaginary number and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/928bc9fa8c0deba11e5af9bef72fe0ffe3990aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Z_1-Z_2|=|Z_2|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />. For any values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/c/28c367151db654c98df81eb7ab6e1d72b4233f10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e2f6d8f31beacce2d10c823fa4d68e278e8f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> that satisfies these conditions we have:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/7/9e7b5a7f95c6a42c8242ba4a5d79afc1ea054d10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mbox{Im}(Z_2)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61b3533556d4058012f0a1e4c61d334a7fdbb160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Im}(Z_2)\\leq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/6/956393db52001013a34954193064163e435e9e7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|Z_1|\\leq2|Z_2|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d2c9742925d19d9d5da678e43ea111942b7746d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Re}(Z_1)\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/6/d365a08c4cf5d99e1174d16c4aa6fe0fa7a1feeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{Re}(Z_1)\\geq\\text{Im}(Z_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"130\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016/Day_1/Problem_3\" title=\"MIE 2016/Day 1/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In the expansion of \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3b10cbea98ac52911f76be1d86026f964411eea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x\\sin2\\beta+\\frac{1}{x}\\cos2\\beta\\right)^{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"185\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>the independent term (in other words, the term without <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />) is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db578fae014527cdd9271bf4aa8ced9027a83c0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63/256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />. With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> being a real number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65810ca742b4fa0d23448d7dee5bde9b7a86cfd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt; \\beta&lt;\\pi/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef232f1c3f50a3c3557f43153502b25dec8d3bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/b/fdb63b9e51abe6bbb16acfb5d7b773ddbb5bf4a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"10\" height=\"16\" /> is:\n</p><p><br />\n(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50f0a7bd40e45cbec6101b343a2c30139496a92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/0/e2049bd6894cfe0b8fe6c83be6b564bf76533f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7325aadaf44259be8452ddedd8264c5ea42e3bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/0/7b0b08fc04a4ff67acc4f8d5cffbece68ce7d3b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44ed4a46e188ab258987ec98094ea8c66f4cad8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\pi}{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"33\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016/Day_1/Problem_4\" title=\"MIE 2016/Day 1/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d59d08e1d527b738154dea64b0ab18f6ce64b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin^4\\alpha+\\cos^4\\alpha}{\\sin^6\\alpha+\\cos^6\\alpha}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"115\" height=\"43\" />, knowing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/6/706979e0d9e9b82ce73616351a0cfb718215a678.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin\\alpha\\cos\\alpha=\\frac{1}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"115\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03afcc71549240237f22ec1edff8b844c69a3fe1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{22}{21}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/d/1bd53b9672e16a490036f04965da63ab27e7bdff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{23}{22}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/3/9d3fec12d09bc002299330ecab4647ec4ca48394.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{23}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57afb8d2a61e812ef37b44ab4c13487a47c87c53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{13}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e927f3485313b83d05596cbdbc6252cb42fb39b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{26}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016/Day_1/Problem_5\" title=\"MIE 2016/Day 1/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/6/97684fa3c73c2bc19aabe99cf703548f4830ecf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\begin{vmatrix}1&amp;a&amp;-2\\\\a-2&amp;1&amp;1\\\\2&amp;-3&amp;1\\end{vmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -28px\" width=\"168\" height=\"65\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/2/022940a765ca072793b00931ceecd0f1a8a073f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/2/3224a48a6a71d173a3ea29033a1e686c9ae692a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{det}(A^2-2A+I)=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"176\" height=\"19\" />. The sum of the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies this condition is:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/2/972f4f8ebd47e06e473ced0d49e77d7f375eceec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{det}(X)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> is the determinant of the matrix <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The product of the real roots of the following equation is equal to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1940821ed63d7d965df162925613e6b53cc1a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^{\\log_3\\sqrt{3y}}=y^{\\log_33y}-6,~~y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"228\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><br />\n(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/1/e1150a17bf1b733cb666be84d920c71fc96bb3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/505bb7b0ab552d846e4d08e3a8393edabaeb19f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\sqrt{|x-1|+|x-2|+|x-3|+...+|x-2017|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"416\" height=\"32\" />. The minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is in the interval:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c3f0cd9ce7d4e89be5190f6dc60180d3363e96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\infty,1008]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75bb7a0261dc6254465d88e70e4e960d0168dc6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1008,1009]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecf6f844c56ebe845852158ed002a6a68904b550.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1009,1010]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/8/0c8b0bdbefe87669231f4d789d7b60c2861cbd5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1010,1011]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/7/e2776a2296d99dd0dcf2cd83fd15ab602918baa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1011,+\\infty)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be complex numbers that satisfies the following system:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33418752fe8730514df7406f22b6449a0d9143c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{cases}x+y+z=7\\\\x^2+y^2+z^2=25\\\\\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{1}{y}+\\frac{1}{z}=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -33px\" width=\"153\" height=\"75\" />\n</p><p><br />\nCompute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/013d9c2c0a44f2b7c486135589b56463a6048c77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+y^3+z^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b4328d77715c539955c57ce1aee7b7bc9cdea458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec670a6cc74a8a120be9f280800052ca2600c563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$235$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0362f8decbd5131e34fd0619f907ecb8be327718.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$320$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/e/3fe560791cab3b11c026775d4377050c0c092be3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$325$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016/Day_1/Problem_9\" title=\"MIE 2016/Day 1/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A hexagon is divided into 6 equilateral triangles. How many ways can we put the numbers from 1 to 6 in each triangle, without repetition, such that the sum of the numbers of three adjacent triangles is always a multiple of 3? Solutions obtained by rotation or reflection are differents, thus the following figures represent two distinct solutions.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:MIE_2016_problem_10.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/6/69/MIE_2016_problem_10.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"252\" height=\"119\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><br />\n(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/367f6b15d47102fd8fdfc1bafed72c1daeadb35a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/43722f5cc8bc044824d4098f0a73e7dd62d9ac98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_2,a_3,a_4,...)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> be an arithmetic progression and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/2/b721297317a9af3b0af3595904e16a182ed9ae82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b_1,b_2,b_3,b_4,...)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" />, an geometric progression of integer terms, of ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30a323a0def6e42553abdcb1326c864d63738a12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/8/fb899c6cacf686ca163e5a9dbfc20513f3e7074b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />. We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06aa5858707e526fa10a690c3d9843ff7afa218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1+b_2=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/d/a0db121c16536268a708322684bf926e7d346a5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_4+b_3=26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"99\" height=\"17\" />. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" /> is:\n</p><p>(a) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(b) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(c) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(d) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>(e) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1_2\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be a 2x2 real matrix . Define a function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> that each element of the matrix moves to the next position in clockwise direction, in other words, if  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/2/662b3de4a94a4dd2d30296eb35e4b1353e61ef13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=\\begin{pmatrix}a&amp;b\\\\c&amp;d\\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"102\" height=\"43\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/754c04b0c96294daf14cd5eb2616082a1e23e9cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(M)=\\begin{pmatrix}c&amp;a\\\\d&amp;b\\end{pmatrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"127\" height=\"43\" />. Find all 2x2 real symmetric matrixes such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8ab3fc3104576b9e28ab5aadf75339809bca0465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M^2=f(M)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Solve the inequation, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec5de01a97e73f9cd6fd0020787398d81801dd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e50bb091712897b8143dd89c18947c0e6f0360c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9x^2}{(1-\\sqrt{3x+1})^2}&gt;4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"156\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3_2\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Solve the system, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b5c9755a11dfd9dea1da1dcd236e268bad8675.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y\\in\\mathbb{R}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dc68935714c017f7e67f93a99b5f2e245f3017d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{cases}\\log_{3}(\\log_{\\sqrt3}x)-\\log_{\\sqrt3}(\\log_{3}y)=1\\\\(y\\sqrt[3]{x})^2=3^{143} \\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"268\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4_2\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=17\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Classify the following system as determined, possible indetermined and impossible according to the real values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107a6e1abcc914573849d3edd1e58a98ae5900f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{cases}(m-2)x+2y-z=m+1\\\\2x+my+2z=m^2+2\\\\2mx+2(m+1)y+(m+1)z=m^3+3\\end{cases}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -34px\" width=\"346\" height=\"77\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5_2\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=18\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b245331cc3cccf7ccaf7e2f6a34fa2131b8b33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/c/f9cf239d12fdb09d8b2bbc145676017e5c038ae4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w=47+ci$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/b/a3bb76f2d707b401b4070b26029357f0be8f175e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^3+w=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, knowing that they are positive integers.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6_2\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=19\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has its vertex at the origin of the cartesian system, its centroid is the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b05710494df8e4fea46e7a3766c769b2952ff80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> and its circumcenter is the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/a/67aca647b04b5fc456670b6779be9a1f2c720f63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E(55/18,5/6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" />. Determine:\n</p>\n<ul><li>The equation of the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c4819459cd27cdcdeff00f11732362285f2ef7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta_{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />;</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The coordinates of the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7_2\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=20\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2c92e5e88c066d6c96487175c9425492666a7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\cos x}{\\cos y}+\\frac{\\sin x}{\\sin y}=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"150\" height=\"40\" />, then compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/1/e31529455bbaf43296e1e8bf8e9e2bf870cf3cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\frac{3\\cos{y}+\\cos{3y}}{\\cos{x}}+\\frac{3\\sin{y}-\\sin{3y}}{\\sin{x}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"295\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8_2\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=21\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<pre>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/3/ce3d85bec6d5f49b084e2908505a0c4415031f32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=\\{1,2,3,4\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />.\n</pre>\n<ul><li>How many function from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> have exactly 2 elements in its image set?</li></ul>\n<ul><li>Between the 256 functions from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, we draw the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, knowing that can have repetition. What's the probability of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/4/30419ef8aa142f637819984019deac7c66495881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$fog$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> be a constant function?</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9_2\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c4819459cd27cdcdeff00f11732362285f2ef7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta_{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be the intern angle bisector such that it's the geometric mean of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />, and the measure of the median <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> is the geometric mean of the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> are on the side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Compute the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c4819459cd27cdcdeff00f11732362285f2ef7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta_{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> em terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10_2\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In a equilateral cone there are two inscribed spheres of radii <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe9b8146945c93b07731ee7f35e017fb2f82204.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt3-1}{\\sqrt3+1}R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"73\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, like in the image. A surface is secant to the cone such that it's tangent to both spheres. Determine in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> the largest segment line that there is between the two points of the curve formed by the intersection of the surface with the cone.\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:MIE_2016_day_2_problem_10.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/2/20/MIE_2016_day_2_problem_10.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"284\" height=\"187\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=MIE_2016&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018093744\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.075 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.093 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 826/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 265/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 27601/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.528      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.528      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15868:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018093744 and revision id 89658. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}